# Daily profile

The Daily profile aligns your days by the time of day, in five-minute periods of
the local day. This shows the patterns at each time of day.

The [Loop Analysis overview](/docs/reports/loop-analysis) tells you about the
filters, net loop correction and how to read the charts. They are the same on
all five pages.

<Screenshot id="loop-analysis-daily-profile" />

The tiles at the top show the totals:

- **Days with data**.
- **Total insulin** each day.
- **Basal / bolus**: the split between basal and bolus.
- **Automatic / manual bolus**.
- **Delivered basal ratio**: delivered basal divided by scheduled basal.
- **Net loop correction** each day.

Four tiles use only complete days: **Total insulin**, **Basal / bolus**,
**Automatic / manual bolus** and **Net loop correction**. A day counts in these
tiles only when the report uses 90% of the day or more. Delivery must also be
known for 90% of the day or more. Known delivery is recorded, or filled from the
schedule. Net loop correction each day also needs the schedule for 90% of the
day. The report never increases a part of a day to a full day. Today counts only when 90% of
the day is before now.

**Days with data** counts each day with glucose or treatments. **Delivered basal
ratio** adds all the days that have delivery and a schedule.

The charts are under the tiles. From top to bottom:

- **Glucose**, with your target range behind it.
- **Basal**: the scheduled basal and the delivered basal.
- **Net loop correction**: the insulin that the loop added or removed. A line
  shows the mean, with automatic boluses. A band shows the middle half of the
  temp basal change only. The chart under it shows the sum of the correction for
  each hour.
- **Insulin on board** and **carbs on board**.
- **Manual boluses** and **carbs**: how frequently and how much at each time of
  day.

<Screenshot id="loop-analysis-daily-glucose" />

To list the days for a time, select the time or press Enter on it. Each day
links to **Day in Review** at that time. A day that the range includes only
partly, for example today, shows **Part of the day**.

